  "priorExpiration": "2004-04-27",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 5506.01 Reasonably Equivalent Offense Hearing.\n\n(a) Pursuant to RSA 651-B:10, any sexual offender or offender against children convicted pursuant to a law of another jurisdiction who wishes to appeal a decision of the division, regarding the division's determination pursuant to Saf-C 5502.02 that the offense is reasonably equivalent to an offense requiring registration under RSA 651-B and these rules, including the duration of the duty to report shall, within 10 days of notification by the division, request a hearing in front of the commissioner.\n\n(b) The scope of the hearing shall be limited to a determination of whether the offense in another jurisdiction is reasonably equivalent to an offense requiring registration under RSA 651-B and these rules.\n\nSource. #7982, INTERIM eff 10-30-03, EXPIRED: 4-27-04\n\nNew. #8083, eff 5-11-04; ss by #10121, eff 4-25-12; ss by #13504, eff 12-9-22",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c5500.html"
